# A1-T01, C2-S01 to C2-S03 — the road, Iron on the Horizon, the Knight-Commander,
# Ironhold Gate. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2078–2204.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/ironhold_gate.tscn (cinematic).
# Source fix: Kaelen recognises Seraphina's VOICE (her cabin cadence), not her
# face. He never really looked at the crew. That's why she has to test him.
# rhythm: clipped commander gate
# (The seat interrogation is a rapid-fire test, and "Later. / Later." is a
# comic beat. Both are meant to be short.)

~ road
Elara: You keep checking the sky. Every few steps, the way Bran checks for rain before he opens the gate.
Kaelen: Habit, I think. Something from the old job. I can't remember what I was waiting to see up there.
Elara: Bad skies where you're from, then?
Kaelen: No. It mostly stayed where you left it. Rained when it said it would, give or take.
Elara: You keep starting to say "airplane" and stopping. What is one, properly?
Kaelen: A metal room full of people. It argues with gravity for a few hours, and it's supposed to win.
Elara: Sounds like it lost the argument.
do kaelen_stops
# He stops walking. She hears what she just said.
Elara: ...Sorry. I said that without thinking.
Kaelen: No, it's— you're right. It lost. I just hadn't heard anyone say it out loud yet.
do walk_on

# C2-S01 — Iron on the Horizon.
~ horizon
do ironhold_reveal
Kaelen (Internal): Workshops at the bottom, market terraces stacked on top, fortress bridges over all of it. And a clock tower you can see from anywhere, whether you want the time or not.
Elara: Try not to insult anyone before we've found a bed and something hot to eat.
Kaelen: I did fine in Oakhaven. Nobody threw anything at me.
Elara: Mara charged you double.
Kaelen: She said double was the friendly rate. I still don't know what strangers pay.
Elara: Strangers get the burnt end and a fair price. Double means she expects you back.
do convoy_passes
Paladin: Children inside the wagons, for me, please! Left side clear! Keep the aisle— keep the centre open!
Kaelen (Internal): Keep the aisle clear...
[if elara_trust_high] Elara: Kaelen? What is it?
[if not elara_trust_high] Elara: Stranger? You've gone pale.
Kaelen: I know that voice. I've heard it tell me to stay in my seat.

# C2-S02 — The Knight-Commander.
~ commander
do seraphina_helmet_off
Seraphina: Move, please. You're standing in the lane, and there are children in the wagon behind you.
Kaelen: I know you. I'm sure I know you.
Seraphina: That line works better without a sword on your hip.
Kaelen: Your voice. You said "keep the aisle—" back there and caught yourself. I've heard you finish it.
Kaelen: Flight 707.
do seraphina_grip
Seraphina: Where did you hear that number?
Kaelen: I was on it.
do pause 1.2
Seraphina: What seat?
Kaelen: What?
Seraphina: Your seat. What was it?
Kaelen: I don't remember.
Seraphina: Row?
Kaelen: I don't—
Seraphina: Window or aisle?
Kaelen: ...Window.
# Her breath catches. She was working the right-hand side that day.
Seraphina: You were there.
Elara: You two know each other?
Seraphina: No.
do pause 0.8
Seraphina: We died together.
do kaelen_still
# She regrets it the moment it's out.
Seraphina: Nearly. I meant nearly.
Kaelen: You had that correction ready. You've said it to someone before.
Seraphina: I've had practice. Behind the last wagon, both of you, please. Keep up.
set ch2_seraphina_met

# C2-S03 — Ironhold Gate. Three queues: residents, traders, Fracture inspection.
~ gate
Gate Officer: Knight-Commander.
Kaelen: Knight-Commander?
Seraphina: Later.
Kaelen: You were a flight attendant.
Seraphina: Later.
Elara: I like her already.
Seraphina: Wait until you've stood in my queues. Two with me, officer, on my count. Inspection line, then residents, please.
do queues
Rook: That crate is medicinal resin. It says so on the side, in letters, which I'd have thought was the cheap way to settle this.
Clerk: It's listed as decorative sap.
Rook: Then whoever wrote that list has never paid for a fever. Ask the lower streets what one costs this month.
# He notices Kaelen. He doesn't introduce himself. He files him away.
Kaelen (Internal): That man just looked me over, boots to sword hilt, like he was working out what I'd fetch.
set ch2_ironhold_entered
